a hundred turns.  With the same character adding a +5 small shield (to go
to AC -48) Orcus did not do any permanent damage over a similar timespan.
He missed a lot more, and did less damage when he hit.

The damage reduction is 3 points per hit (which can apply to perhaps 20
attacks during one turn if you're surrounded) -- but more important are
the added *misses*.  These become significant against the toughest
monsters as AC approaches -50.

I've run a wizmode test, based on the YANI given (that wizards should be
able to enchant armor a little higher.)  Details as to where each of these
